# <Troubleshooting & Gotchas>

<Punchline: Quick-reference diagnostic commands and symptom-to-fix tables to resolve authentication errors, expired tokens, and network timeouts in under 2 minutes.>

> [!TIP]
> **First Diagnostic Check**: Before troubleshooting deeper, verify connectivity and active identity:
> ```bash
> curl -sSf https://api.internal/healthz && auth-cli whoami
> ```

---

## Symptom, Cause & Resolution Matrix

| Symptom / Error Message | Probable Root Cause | Resolution / Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `401 Unauthorized: token_expired` | Access token exceeded 60-minute TTL. | Run `auth-cli refresh` to mint a fresh JWT, or verify client clock skew. |
| `403 Forbidden: insufficient_scope` | Token lacks `write:deployments` role. | Request role elevation in `#access-mgmt` and verify via `auth-cli inspect --token $TOKEN`. |
| `504 Gateway Timeout on /v2/query` | Connection pool saturation under load. | Increase max pool size in `config.yaml` (`pool_size: 50`) and scale worker replicas. |
| `EADDRINUSE: port 8080` | Stale orphan process holding the port. | Execute `lsof -ti:8080 | xargs kill -9` and restart the local dev server. |

